<section class="sec tint"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-head left rv"><p class="kicker">Regions</p><h2>How claims differ across Illinois</h2><p>The same policy wording plays out very differently in a Chicago two-flat, a Naperville cul-de-sac and a farmhouse outside Carbondale.</p></div><div class="ilist" data-stagger><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/chicago-night-aerial.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/chicago-night-aerial-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/chicago-night-aerial.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><small>Bungalows, two-flats, towers</small><h2>Chicago &amp; Cook County</h2><p>Combined sewers, brick bungalows and lakefront condos. Basement backups after summer cloudbursts and pipes split by polar-vortex cold are as common here as storm damage.</p></span></div><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/suburban-street.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/suburban-street-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/suburban-street.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1024" height="768" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><small>DuPage · Kane · Lake · McHenry · Will</small><h2>Collar counties</h2><p>Subdivisions and townhome associations from Naperville to Waukegan. One hail swath can touch dozens of buildings under a single master policy.</p></span></div><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/snowy-suburban-home.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/snowy-suburban-home-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/snowy-suburban-home.webp 1024w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1024" height="683" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><small>Rockford · Elgin · Rock River Valley</small><h2>Northern Illinois</h2><p>Long winters bring ice dams and snow load; spring brings tornadoes like the 2023 Belvidere storm. Older housing stock adds plaster and wood-siding matching questions.</p></span></div><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/prairie-supercell.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/prairie-supercell-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/prairie-supercell.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1200" height="658" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><small>Peoria · Springfield · Bloomington · Champaign</small><h2>Central Illinois</h2><p>Open prairie lets storms arrive at full strength. Washington in 2013 and Springfield in 2006 show how severe central Illinois tornadoes can be.</p></span></div><div class="icard rv"><span class="icard-ph"><img src="/assets/img/photos/tornado-debris-field.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/tornado-debris-field-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/tornado-debris-field.webp 1200w" sizes="(max-width:700px) 100vw, 260px" width="1200" height="900" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span><span class="icard-b"><small>Belleville · Edwardsville · Carbondale</small><h2>Metro East &amp; Southern Illinois</h2><p>From the 1925 Tri-State Tornado to the 2009 derecho, southern Illinois has a long wind history — and sits near the New Madrid seismic zone.</p></span></div></div></div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="wrap band-in rv"><div><h2>Don’t see your city?</h2><p>We cover every Illinois county. Call and tell us where the property is.</p></div><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn dark" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn line-dark" href="/contact-an-appraiser/">Email the estimate</a></div></div></section>
